pillars='''const antifragility: [string, string, string][] = [["Redundancy", "Never let one server, data center, or routing vendor hold the keys to critical life support.", "Municipal utilities, hospitals, and air transit networks need secondary and tertiary failover systems that activate instantly."], ["Offline + air-gapped backups", "Critical information must not exist solely in the cloud.", "Medical histories, land titles, legal records, and emergency manuals need immutable physical or local copies disconnected from the public internet."], ["Alternative + analog communication", "When fiber cables and cell towers fail, voice and emergency dispatch cannot go silent.", "Maintain HAM networks, high-frequency transceivers, mesh radios, and point-to-point satellite links dedicated to disaster recovery."], ["Resilient + microgrid power", "Information technology is dead silicon without electricity.", "Water plants, trauma centers, and telecom hubs need solar, geothermal, hydrogen, or other decentralized power that survives national-grid failures."], ["Human + manual skills", "Software should assist people, never replace capability entirely.", "Pilots, railway managers, grid dispatchers, and surgeons need mandatory analog drills with valves, charts, and manual switches."], ["Hardened cyber-physical security", "Treat critical civic infrastructure as sovereign defense ground.", "Disconnect grids, water plants, and nuclear systems from public access; enforce Zero Trust hardware authentication and post-quantum protocols."], ["Responsible AI + oversight", "Never surrender final life-or-death decisions to opaque automation.", "Infrastructure, medical, and emergency systems need fail-safe testing, legal accountability, and non-bypassable manual kill switches."], ["Radical decentralization", "Avoid hyper-centralized monopolistic choke points.", "Invest in open protocols, municipal software stacks, and distributed data architectures instead of a handful of hyperscalers."]];\n\n'''
